name>Dalmeijer</surname><given-names>RAJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>In vitro and in vivo degradation of biomimetic octacalcium phosphate and carbonate apatite coatings on titanium implants</article-title><source>J Biomed Mater Res A</source><year>2003b</year><volume>64A</volume><fpage>378</fpage><lpage>87</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Basle</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Chappard</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Grizon</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Osteoclastic resorption of Ca-P biomaterials implanted in rabbit bone</article-title><source>Calcif Tissue Int</source><year>1993</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>348</fpage><lpage>56</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8287324</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bellows</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name><name><surname>Heersche</surname><given-names>JN</given-names></name><name><surname>Aubin</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inorganic phosphate added exogenously or released from beta-glycerophosphate initiates mineralization of osteoid nodules in vitro</article-title><source>Bone Miner</source><year>1992</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>15</fpage><lpage>29</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1581703</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Berube</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Carnes</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The effect of sputtered calcium phosphate coatings of different crystallinity on osteoblast differentiation</article